  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OpenCRVS support for country implementation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will further develop the OpenCRVS product and take it to scale through the formation of a vibrant community of governments, development partners, system integrators and software developers. This will contribute to significant improvements in the quality of civil registration systems around the world and make them more affordable and sustainable, even in the lowest resource settings. Over time these systems will help establish universal legal identity, support government service delivery and provide accurate population data, ensuring that all individuals are recognised, protected and provided for from birth. This is of articualr importance for the borad inclusion of marginalized groups and for gender equality, for example through access to public services.</narrative>
  </description>
